From eceead395b5ac1e0eed864fe901d5aee5c3da240 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 19:06:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 21/40] configs: exynos9820-beyond2lte: give the heap room for
 a sparse write

Flashing a sparse image over fastboot fails on the very first chunk,
whatever its size, with "Malloc failed for: CHUNK_TYPE_RAW".  The size of
the chunk is a red herring: what fails is a buffer the sparse writer
allocates once, and it is sized from the device, not from the chunk.

lib/image-sparse.c asks for FASTBOOT_MAX_BLK_WRITE blocks of bounce buffer
whenever the data cache is on, and that constant is 16384.  The storage of
this board hands out blocks of 4096 bytes, so the request is 64 MiB against
a heap of 32.  It can never succeed, which is why chunks of 128, 32, 8 and
2 MiB all failed the same way.

A second buffer can be live at the same time: the block backend falls back
to writing zeros when the device has no erase operation, and that one asks
for FASTBOOT_MAX_BLOCKS_SOFT_ERASE blocks, another 16 MiB.  So the worst
case is 80 MiB of buffers plus everything else the loader keeps on the
heap.

128 MiB leaves room for both and for growth.  Memory is not the scarce
thing here: this phone has eight gigabytes and the loader already stops
itself at the four gigabyte line for the sake of the storage controller.

What this buys is not a tidier log.  Without it the only way to put an
image on this phone is the vendor tool, which needs a person holding the
phone in download mode; with it the whole loop can run from the host over
the cable.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 configs/exynos9820-beyond2lte_defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/configs/exynos9820-beyond2lte_defconfig b/configs/exynos9820-beyond2lte_defconfig
index 334a48f8..3c63f416 100644
--- a/configs/exynos9820-beyond2lte_defconfig
+++ b/configs/exynos9820-beyond2lte_defconfig
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@ CONFIG_SKIP_LOWLEVEL_INIT=y
 CONFIG_COUNTER_FREQUENCY=26000000
 CONFIG_POSITION_INDEPENDENT=y
 CONFIG_ARCH_EXYNOS=y
-CONFIG_SYS_MALLOC_LEN=0x2000000
+CONFIG_SYS_MALLOC_LEN=0x8000000
 CONFIG_SYS_MALLOC_F_LEN=0x16000
 CONFIG_TARGET_EXYNOS_MOBILE=y
 CONFIG_NR_DRAM_BANKS=6
